---
description: Citation and bibliography hygiene for technical papers
globs: papers/**/*.{bib,md,tex}
alwaysApply: false
---

When working on citations:

- Never invent papers, authors, years, venues, or DOIs.
- Prefer BibTeX entries the author can verify.
- Use stable citation keys: `AuthorYYYYShortTitle` or existing project convention.
- Ensure every strong claim in the draft has a supporting citation or experiment.
- Flag missing related work categories: closest baseline, classical foundation, concurrent work.
- Prefer primary sources over blogs when both exist.
- Keep `references.bib` free of unused junk when preparing submission, unless the author wants a working library.
